0343: SapphireGpu: clocks, DDR and temperatures, measured (read only): kern.sweet_gpu_clocks, kern.sweet_ddr_khz, kern.sweet_thermal, kern.sweet_gpu_temp

Read only: nothing changes what a block does, and nothing runs unless a sysctl is read (or boot-arg
gpu_clkdiag=1 prints both lines after the GPU powers up).

- kern.sweet_gpu_clocks (string, ~0.2 s): gx_gfx3d and cx_gmu through the GPU CC debug mux,
  gcc_gpu_memnoc_gfx and gcc_bimc_gpu_axi through the GCC's, both CPU clusters through the APSS mux, and the
  DDR from the memory controller's period register, with Qualcomm's clock measurement as the stock
  debugcc-khaje.c / clk-debug.c do it (muxes and inputs from debugcc-khaje.c). Debug branches and the XO/4
  branch are left as found. Before the GPU is powered it gives only the DDR.
- kern.sweet_ddr_khz (int): 10^12 / the period in ps at 0x447d220 (mccc_debug of the stock device tree).
- kern.sweet_thermal (string): the 16 TSENS sensors (SROT 0x4410000, TM 0x4411000; tsens2xxx.c / Linux
  tsens-v2.c), each by the name of the stock thermal zone that uses it, in milli-degrees C, with SROT_CTRL
  and TM_TRDY; values outside -40..150 C are not valid. kern.sweet_gpu_temp (int): sensor 15, the stock
  "gpu" zone; ENODEV, EAGAIN (first round not complete) or EIO (no valid value).

Locking: the clock measurement runs under its own lock (clk_lock); its pages are mapped once on first use.
TSENS and the DDR period are plain reads.

Measured on the phone at boot: gx_gfx3d 819998 kHz (gpu_mhz=820), DDR 1555210 kHz, CPU clusters 2803196
and 1900802 kHz; one minute after boot the 16 sensors read 65.6-70.2 C. No hang reading any of them.

